        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "66ff089b-86c1-531d-adf3-5164d6782ca1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Events: 1996 PGA Championship, 2000 PGA Championship, 2014 PGA Championship, 2008 Ryder Cup\n- Places: Valhalla Golf Club, Louisville, Kentucky\n- People: Mark Brooks, Kenny Perry, Tiger Woods, Bob May\n\nFacts:\n- The 1996 PGA Championship was the 78th PGA Championship and was held August 8–11 at Valhalla Golf Club in Louisville, Kentucky.\n- Mark Brooks won the 1996 PGA Championship, his only major championship, with a birdie on the first hole of a sudden-death playoff against Kenny Perry.\n- The 2000 PGA Championship was the 82nd PGA Championship and was held August 17–20 at Valhalla Golf Club in Louisville, Kentucky.\n- Tiger Woods won the 2000 PGA Championship, his second straight PGA Championship and fifth major, in a three-hole playoff over Bob May.\n- The 2014 PGA Championship was the third PGA Championship held at Valhalla Golf Club, following the 1996 and 2000 editions.\n- Valhalla Golf Club also hosted the Ryder Cup in 2008, which was the most recent U.S. victory in that event mentioned here.\n- Both the 1996 and 2000 PGA Championships at Valhalla Golf Club were decided in playoffs.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "6f52bbcd-72ce-568b-89cd-edc32079ba27",
        "text": "Page: 1996 PGA Championship. Sentence: The 1996 PGA Championship was the 78th PGA Championship, held August 8–11 at Valhalla Golf Club in Louisville, Kentucky.\nPage: 1996 PGA Championship. Sentence: Mark Brooks won his only major championship with a birdie at the first hole of a sudden-death playoff with Kentucky native Kenny Perry.\nPage: 2000 PGA Championship. Sentence: The 2000 PGA Championship was the 82nd PGA Championship, held August 17–20 at the Valhalla Golf Club in Louisville, Kentucky.\nPage: 2000 PGA Championship. Sentence: Tiger Woods won his second straight PGA Championship and fifth major in a three-hole playoff over Bob May.\nPage: 2014 PGA Championship. Sentence: This was the third PGA Championship at Valhalla, which previously hosted in 1996 and 2000, both won in playoffs, as well as the Ryder Cup in 2008, the most recent U.S. victory.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
